{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `commitAndPushToBaseBranch.js` is a fifth commit-producing staging site outside this canonical list**

The doc claim on this line — "Every commit-producing staging site … builds its commands from this single canonical list" (and the PR description's "All four commit-producing staging sites now exclude …") — is inaccurate repo-wide. `js/commitAndPushToBaseBranch.js` (the generic direct-push postJSAction) still stages broadly with no untrack cleanup:

```js
// js/commitAndPushToBaseBranch.js:106-109
runCmd({ command: 'git add -A -- ":!factory-kit" ":!factory-kit/**"' });
runCmd({ command: 'git commit -m "' + message.replace(/"/g, '\\"') + '" --no-verify' });
runCmd({ command: 'git pull --rebase origin ' + baseBranch });
runCmd({ command: 'git push origin HEAD:' + baseBranch });   // straight onto the base branch
```

It has **no** `git rm -r --cached` self-heal and **no** `:!.dmtools/...` pathspecs. Target repos don't carry this repo's new `.gitignore`, so if this flow is ever wired up, any on-disk runtime log (`.dmtools/credential-helper.log`, `fa-trace.log`, the full session store) gets committed **and pushed directly to the target repo's default branch** — the worst-case variant of the gh-628 leak this PR exists to close.

**Why not blocking**: today nothing references it — `grep -r commitAndPushToBaseBranch` matches only the module itself, and no agent config sets `customParams.directPush`. Latent debt, not a live leak.

**Suggested fix** (2 lines, keeps the list canonical):

```js
var gitStaging = require('./common/gitStaging.js');
// …
runCmd({ command: gitStaging.buildUntrackCommand() });
runCmd({ command: 'git add -A -- ' + gitStaging.buildStagingPathspecs() +
    ' ":!factory-kit" ":!factory-kit/**"' });
```

…or, if the direct-push flow is intentionally retired, delete the module so the "every commit-producing staging site" claim becomes true by construction. (Adding it here would also deserve a unit test mirroring the other four sites' gh-628 assertions.)
