{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `.gitignore` carries only 6 of the 7 canonical artifacts — and nothing pins the two lists together**

`RUNTIME_ARTIFACT_PATHS` in `js/common/gitStaging.js` has 7 entries; the `.gitignore` block added in this PR has 6 — `.dmtools/copilot-sessions/` is absent. Self-host legs run inside *this* repo (that's exactly how gh-628 happened), so a leftover `.dmtools/copilot-sessions/` shows up as `??` noise to any plain `git status` / `git add .` here — the same class the other six entries guard against.

Also, the round-3 resolution stated "the new suite cross-checks" the `.gitignore` copy — it doesn't: `test_gitStaging.js` pins the module against its own inline `ALL_ARTIFACTS` duplicate, not against `.gitignore`, so the two lists can still drift silently (the very drift class this module was extracted to kill).

Either add `.dmtools/copilot-sessions/` to `.gitignore`, or (better) pin the pair with a small test that reads `.gitignore` and asserts every `RUNTIME_ARTIFACT_PATHS` entry is represented:

```js
var gitignore = file_read({ path: '.gitignore' }) || '';
for (var i = 0; i < gitStaging.RUNTIME_ARTIFACT_PATHS.length; i++) {
    assert.contains(gitignore, gitStaging.RUNTIME_ARTIFACT_PATHS[i],
        '.gitignore must ignore ' + gitStaging.RUNTIME_ARTIFACT_PATHS[i]);
}
```
